=== Prompt ===
Who is Geralt of Rivia?

=== Response ===
Geralt of Rivia is the main protagonist in a popular fantasy series of novels, short stories, and video games. He is a Witcher, a genetically enhanced human trained to hunt monsters and mutated creatures for a living.

In the books, written by Polish author Andrzej Sapkowski, Geralt is a mutated human, born with supernatural abilities due to his exposure to a powerful potion during his mother's pregnancy. These mutations give him enhanced strength, agility, and reflexes, as well as the ability to develop supernatural senses and skills, such as his iconic silver swordsmanship and his ability to see and track supernatural creatures.

Geralt's profession as a Witcher is to hunt monsters and other creatures that threaten the people of the Continent, a medieval-inspired world filled with magic, mythical creatures, and politics. He operates on a moral code, taking on contracts from those who need his services, but refusing to kill humans, unless absolutely necessary.

Geralt is known for his stoicism, his dry sense of humor, and his complex moral code, which often puts him at odds with the people around him. He is a solitary figure, preferring to keep to himself, but he is also fiercely loyal to those he cares about.

The Witcher series has been adapted into several video games, including the popular action role-playing games "The Witcher" (2007), "The Witcher 2: Assassins of Kings" (2011), and "The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt" (2015), which are widely considered to be some of the best games of all time.

The series has also been adapted into a Netflix original series, "The Witcher," which premiered in 2019, starring Henry Cavill as Geralt of Rivia.

Overall, Geralt of Rivia is a complex and intriguing character, who has captured the hearts of fans around the world with his unique blend of wit, wisdom, and deadly skill.

